[Music]  while we wait for official avengers 4  news from the notoriously tight-lipped  crew at marvel here's a look at why  captain america is crucial to the  outcome of the war against  thanos and whether he'll still be  standing when those end credits roll  the biggest news to break regarding  captain america since the epic final  moments of infinity war  came to us in the form of a quick  goodbye note tweeted by none other than  chris evans himself  in only a few heartfelt words evans let  the whole world know that he would be  putting down his shield for good the  tweet which amassed  several hundred thousand likes within  hours read officially wrapped on  avengers 4.  it was an emotional day to say the least  playing this role over the last eight  years has been  an honor to everyone in front of the  camera behind the camera and  in the audience thank you for the  memories eternally grateful  maybe we'll see a cameo or two down the  road but for all intents and purposes  it does seem like this is the end for  steve rogers  infinity war might have been one of the  wildest rides in cinema history but  captain america's role in it was  actually  fairly minor sure we got a fun  re-emergent sequence for cap in the  fight at the train station in edinburgh  and his attempt to rally a crew of  heroes together to defend the world  against bad guys was a crucial part of  the plot  but even if captain america ultimately  received a decent amount of screen time  it did feel a bit like he was being used  to move the story forward more than  anything else  earth just lost your best defender so  we're here to fight  [Music]  and if you want to stand in our way  we'll fight you too the truth is captain  america ended up having a muted role in  infinity war the story had him stranded  in the middle of a sidebar conflict in  wakanda while  iron man took front and center on titan  it stands to reason that this will set  steve rogers up to be a crucial element  in the next chapter  where we'll almost certainly see more of  cap's storyline unfold  captain america civil war ended on a  pretty low note and many fans were  hoping for some on-screen  reconciliation between steve rogers and  tony stark in infinity war  in the end the two didn't even share a  scene the avengers broke up  we're toast broke up  like a band like like the beatles that's  not to say that the folks behind the  scenes didn't try to fit it in writer  stephen mcfeely explained that in the  original drafts of the script they had  steve and tony in the same room together  ultimately however he said as many times  as we wrote those scenes it became clear  that this movie needed to be propulsive  and be about thanos and what he  represented to the avengers  it may not have fit into infinity wars  plot but there's no way these two aren't  sharing some screen time in avengers 4.  their long-anticipated reconciliation  will no doubt be a pivotal scene and one  that sadly paves the way for cap's  demise  because once that breach is healed cap's  character arc will be nearly complete  just like a few of the other key players  in the mcu captain america's story arc  is in desperate need of closure  we've watched him rise up to lead the  avengers before entering into a  self-imposed exile  only to resurface for infinity war but  the character is still in need of a  final act to bring his story to an end  the russo brothers have been quiet about  what might happen after the third  avengers  only suggesting that infinity war was  quote the next  chapter so to speak in his specific  story and there's been no talk about  where we go beyond that yet  that comment could quite easily be used  to infer that after infinity war there  just  isn't much more left for steve rogers to  do in the mcu  one way or another he needs some closure  family  stability who wanted all that went in  the ice 75 years ago  i think someone else came out the truth  is steve rogers doesn't really have to  die in avengers 4 for a story arc to  wrap up  for chris evans to move on and for the  universe to be saved the only thing that  seems inevitable is that the character  won't be with us on a regular basis  during phase 4 of the mcu  how could this happen without a  heart-wrenching death scene rogers just  needs to pass the captain america torch  onto a successor  which could just as easily take place  after an epic comeback victory against  the mad titan there's a lot to be said  for quitting while you're ahead and how  much further ahead do you get than  defeating thanos  there's no shortage of rumors floating  about regarding who could replace steve  rogers as captain america whether it's  bucky barnes  sam wilson or even a complete wild card  chances are the mantle of captain  america will be passed on  the question is will steve rogers live  to see the passing of the torch or will  it be wrenched from his grasp  by thanos's hands

